            <ArticleTitle>IgG4-Related Pancreatitis and Immune Thrombocytopenia: A Case Report and Literature Review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1724</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7759/cureus.1724</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a prior diagnosis of IgG4-related autoimmune pancreatitis (AIP) presented four years later with severe prednisone resistant immune thrombocytopenia (ITP). Her case is reported and the scant literature of the very unusual possible association of IgG4-related AIP and ITP is reviewed. It is suggested that investigation for IgG4-related disease be part of the work-up of ITP.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
